Z||000000||Pretender||03-22-99||10:48 PM||||i noticed that the recall campaign 88-C-24 should of been done to my car...my vin number falls between the given numbers....so i took it to the dealership and told them about it..he typed it up on the comp. and told me that it wasnt avail. or had already been performed....But there is no sticker stating this and there is a lack of heat shielding that my mechanic even said should be there.....i think the dealership just doesn't want to do it because of the price and labor involved....what should i do?.........thanks.<br>
Z||000001||swampgas||03-23-99||03:40 PM||||You can call 1-800-GMCARES and they will tell you whether the recall was done on your car. I think the dealers are happy to do it if it needs it. They get paid by the factory. Chances are it was done. I don't have any stickers on mine either and I bought it almost new and know all the recalls were done. Only have one sticker and it's in the glove box.
